Acfda","two"],["לְמַלְכוּת","lemalkhut","H4437","AR/Ncfsc","of [the] reign of"],["דָּרְיָוֶשׁ","dareyavesh","H1868","ANpm","Darius"],["מֶלֶךְ","melekh-","H4430","ANcbsc","[the] king of"],["פָּרָס","paras","H6540","ANpl","Persia"]],"x":[[37001015,37001015,3]],"xn":1}},"people":[{"id":"benjamin_463","name":"Benjamin","also":"Ben-oni","summary":"The younger son of Jacob by Rachel (Gen. 35:18). His birth took place at Ephrath, on the road between Bethel and Bethlehem, at a short distance from the latter place.","verses":157,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[1]},{"id":"zerubbabel_3054","name":"Zerubbabel","also":"Sheshbazzar, Zorobabel","summary":"The seed of Babylon, the son of Salathiel or Shealtiel (Hag. 1:1; Zorobabel, Matt. 1:12); called also the son of Pedaiah (1 Chr. 3:17-19), i.e., according to a frequent usage of the word “son;” the grandson or the nephew of Salathiel.","verses":27,"father":"Pedaiah","mother":"","v":[2,3]},{"id":"esar-haddon_1215","name":"Esar-haddon","also":"","summary":"","verses":3,"father":"Sennacherib","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"joshua_893","name":"Joshua","also":"Jeshua","summary":"The son of Jozadak, and high priest of the Jews under Zerubbabel (Neh. 7:7; 12:1, 7, 10, 26); called Joshua (Hag. 1:1, 12; 2:2, 4; Zech. 3:1, 3, 6, 8, 9).","verses":21,"father":"Josedech","mother":"","v":[3]},{"id":"cyrus_968","name":"Cyrus","also":"","summary":"(Heb. Ko’resh), the celebrated “King of Persia” (Elam) who was conqueror of Babylon, and issued the decree of liberation to the Jews (Ezra 1:1, 2).","verses":19,"father":"","mother":"","v":[3,5]},{"id":"darius_978","name":"Darius","also":"","summary":"King of Persia.","verses":16,"father":"","mother":"","v":[5,24]},{"id":"ahasuerus_117","name":"Ahasuerus","also":"","summary":"The son of Darius Hystaspes, the king named in the Book of Esther. He ruled over the kingdoms of Persia, Media, and Babylonia, “from India to Ethiopia.”","verses":29,"father":"","mother":"","v":[6]},{"id":"artaxerxes_313","name":"Artaxerxes","also":"","summary":"The king who obstructed the rebuilding of the temple (Ezra 4:7).","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[7,8,11]},{"id":"bishlam_515","name":"Bishlam","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"mithredath_2098","name":"Mithredath","also":"","summary":"Persian officer in Samaria.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"tabeel_2809","name":"Tabeel","also":"","summary":"A Persian governor of Samaria, who joined others in the attempt to prevent the rebuilding of Jerusalem (Ezra 4:7).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"rehum_2414","name":"Rehum","also":"","summary":"The “chancellor” of Artaxerxes, who sought to stir him up against the Jews (Ezra 4:8-24) and prevent the rebuilding of the walls and the temple of Jerusalem.","verses":4,"father":"","mother":"","v":[8,9,17,23]},{"id":"shimshai_2707","name":"Shimshai","also":"","summary":"The shining one, or sunny, the secretary of Rehum the chancellor, who took part in opposing the rebuilding of the temple after the Captivity (Ezra 4:8, 9, 17-23).","verses":4,"father":"","mother":"","v":[8,9,17,23]},{"id":"asnappar_346","name":"Asnappar","also":"","summary":"Probably the same as Assur-bani-pal (Sardanapalos of the Greeks), styled the “great and noble” (Ezra 4:10), was the son and successor (B.C. 668) of Esar-haddon.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[10]}],"places":[{"id":"assyria_111","name":"Assyria","kind":"Region","lat":36.50969,"lon":43.2282,"summary":"The name derived from the city Asshur on the Tigris, the original capital of the country, was originally a colony from Babylonia, and was ruled by viceroys from that kingdom.","verses":116,"v":[2]},{"id":"persia_938","name":"Persia","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":34.79831,"lon":48.51497,"summary":"An ancient empire, extending from the Indus to Thrace, and from the Caspian Sea to the Red Sea and the Persian Gulf. The Persians were originally a Medic tribe which settled in Persia, on the eastern side of the Persian Gulf.","verses":25,"v":[3,5,7,24]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[6,8,12,20,23,24]},{"id":"erech_407","name":"Erech","kind":"City","lat":32.32222,"lon":45.63611,"summary":"(LXX., “Orech”), length, or Moon-town, one of the cities of Nimrod’s kingdom in the plain of Shinar (Gen. 10:10); the Orchoe of the Greeks and Romans.","verses":2,"v":[9]},{"id":"susa_1118","name":"Susa","kind":"City","lat":32.19202,"lon":48.24854,"summary":"A lily, the Susa of Greek and Roman writers, once the capital of Elam. It lay in the uplands of Susiana, on the east of the Tigris, about 150 miles to the north of the head of the Persian Gulf.","verses":20,"v":[9]},{"id":"river_244","name":"river","kind":"Region","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"region","verses":16,"v":[10,11,16,17,20]},{"id":"samaria_1022","name":"Samaria","kind":"Region","lat":32.33142,"lon":35.22859,"summary":"A watch-mountain or a watch-tower. In the heart of the mountains of Israel, a few miles north-west of Shechem, stands the “hill of Shomeron,” a solitary mountain, a great “mamelon.”","verses":114,"v":[10,17]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[6862,6862,6862,3063,3063,1144,1144,8085,3588,1121,1121,1129,1129,1964,1964,3068,3068,3068,430,430,3478,3478],[5066,5066,2216,7218,7218,7218,1,1,1,559,1129,1129,1129,5973,5973,3588,0,0,1875,1875,430,430,2076,2076,2076,2076,3808,3808,3808,3117,3117,4428,4428,634,804,804,5927,5927,853,6311],[2216,2216,3442,7605,7605,7605,7218,1,1,1,3478,3478,559,3808,3808,3808,0,0,0,1129,1129,1004,1004,430,430,430,3588,587,3162,1129,1129,3068,3068,3068,3068,430,430,3478,3478,834,3566,4428,6539,6539,6680,6680,6680],[1961,5971,5971,776,776,776,7503,7503,7503,7503